"_about": "Kirsopp Lake’s footnotes to his Greek text (C the Codex Constantinopolitanus, the one complete manuscript), and in \"refs\" the passages of Scripture he prints in the margin (with the digital file’s own reference, \"urn\"). The digital file has only the Greek pages, so the footnotes Lake prints under his English translation on the facing pages are not here. \"at\" is the verse the note or reference stands in (\"title\": the title above the greeting). Greek inside a note is in Beta Code, as in the digital file (so h(mw=n = ἡμῶν), and the file has slips in the notes’ English and Greek. From First1KGreek (Open Greek and Latin), CC BY-SA 4.0.",
"notes": [
{
"at": "1:5",
"note": "This passage is found in the 4th mandate of Hermas, and suggests that this part of the Didache is later than Hermas (c. 140 A. D)."
},
{
"at": "4:3",
"note": "The editors usually emend to poih/seis \"make.\""
},
{
"at": "9:2",
"note": "It is notesorthy that this ordor \"first the Cup\" is only found elseshere in the earliest text of Le. 22, 17 ff, (shich omits v. 20) and perhaps in l. Cor. 10, 16."
},
{
"at": "9:4",
"note": "to/ om. C."
},
